) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which \n19:## 2. Section plan (what each part says; page split is the venue's call)\n47:Evidence: error vs k with CIs on (a) the group-held-out split **scored on the common target set (§2b)**, (b) the fixed subset of models eligible at k_max (≥ k_max observed cells in C and ≥ m_T in T, in the same splits), so the model set does not change\n62:Evidence: unit test (passes: with known parameters the posterior covariance does not depend on y); adaptive (S7) vs batch on the synthetic ladder and the real matrix. Short section or appendix, depending on the venue's budget and on whether any gain shows u\n81:Venue (`venue-repo`#2): NeurIPS 2026 main track, **9 content pages including figures and tables** (references, appendix, checklist excluded), 5.5 in text width. Venue's final answer: from 21 accepted NeurIPS evaluation/benchmark papers, median 6 figures+tab\n85:| **Fig. 1** | Error vs k on held-out groups, common-target-set score (§2b): S6+P5, random-k (mean + spread over C/T splits and draws), best-baseline pipeline, mean-offset baseline, the floor, and (if defensible) the predicted curve from T1; raw points and\n86:| **Fig. 2** | Matrix structure: the spectrum with the noise reference and the three rank estimates (coverage/missingness pattern goes to the appendix) | C1 | half width |\n87:| **Fig. 3** | Theory vs measurement: synthetic (known truth), predicted vs measured with the estimation term vs M; real-data residual = misfit | C4 | one panel per regime: separated factors, decaying spectrum, real |\n88:| **Fig. 4** | Scope map: headline quantity vs each condition (extrapolation, missing rate, M, transform, granularity, ladder with the real matrix placed by the §3-C6 rule) | C6 | small multiples; same y-axis where comparable; the old Fig. 5 |\n89:| **Table 1** | Coverage-filter table and final shape, held-out group counts per split | G1/G4 | mandatory; may be compressed |\n90:| **Table 2** | Primary contrast at k ∈ {1,2,3,5,8,12,20} with CIs and verdicts; the predicted vs empirical k*(ε) at ε = δ, 2δ with CIs | C3, C4 | merges the old Table 3 |\n91:| **Table 3** | Pipeline comparison: inference rules P0–P6 × {random-k, S6} at 3–4 k values, best-of-column marked | C3 | from review #3 |\n94:If the text does not fit, cut in this order (first first): Table 3 merges into Table 2 (the pipeline comparison becomes extra rows at fewer k values), Table 1 is compressed, Fig. 4 becomes a table row set, Fig. 2 becomes a half-width panel of Fig. 3. Fig. 1\n99:- **venue-repo**: answered: NeurIPS 2026, 9 pages, about 4 figures + 3 tables; §5 follows it. Still open: the confirmed budget from accepted papers.\n105:The outline changes when (a) a gate trips, (b) a verdict picks a branch of C3, (c) a claim's evidence cannot be produced, (d) the venue's budget changes §5. It does not change to record each result; results go to the paper. The abstract and the introducti\n111:- rev. 4: aligned with Brief rev. 5 and review #4 (common target set in §1, C2, floor/eligibility, T1 prediction computed on T); venue's final budget (≤ 7 figures+tables; sacrifice order revised; limits in the main text).\n112:- rev. 5: k*(ε) on the excess over the floor, realised shape and the granularity caveat in G1 (from the pre-registration and Brief rev. 6).\n113:- rev. 6: branches taken from the interim results (`story-repo`#5): C1 ambiguous rank; C2 headline as k*(ε) against ε (pre-set ε unreachable, margins labelled); C3 branch A with the scale stated and cross-rule claims on excess over own floor; C4 failure\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "506367d9-b480-5ca7-822c-7ead4f4ca1db", "at": 1795731700.0065677, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 23240, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "1c6116816ae8f61fd18cfac47c3a90ef", "trust": 